{"parentUuid":"c23078aa-6f2d-40e2-86b4-48fcc37005bd","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"13d226c2-7030-46b3-a4a1-d92d92be18ee","agentId":"a6c3a5f3d9dc7d7f6","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SXNNdbMnMMeSXnKHNn3r94","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"Trial credit for GenAI App Builder\" $1000 promotional credit eligible products 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"No one is talking about how to use the Credits of Trial credit for GenAI App Builder - Gemini API - Google AI Developers Forum\",\"url\":\"https://discuss.ai.google.dev/t/no-one-is-talking-about-how-to-use-the-credits-of-trial-credit-for-genai-app-builder/101423\"},{\"title\":\"Clarification on $1000 GenAI App Builder Credit Source - Cloud Foundations & Onboarding - Google Developer forums\",\"url\":\"https://discuss.google.dev/t/clarification-on-1000-genai-app-builder-credit-source/350894\"},{\"title\":\"Google Cloud Gen AI $1000 Fast-Start Program\",\"url\":\"https://cloudcredits.io/providers/gcp/programs/google-cloud-gen-ai-fast-start-program\"},{\"title\":\"Agent Search pricing | Google Cloud\",\"url\":\"https://cloud.google.com/generative-ai-app-builder/pricing\"},{\"title\":\"Google AI Studio do not use my $1300 credits shown on Google Cloud - Gemini API - Google AI Developers Forum\",\"url\":\"https://discuss.ai.google.dev/t/google-ai-studio-do-not-use-my-1300-credits-shown-on-google-cloud/140442\"},{\"title\":\"Google Cloud GenAI App Builder trial credit usage?\",\"url\":\"https://www.facebook.com/groups/vibecodinglife/posts/1992759101312617/\"},{\"title\":\"It’s about **understanding how different Google Cloud and GenAI credits are applied, which services they cover, and how to ensure your AI Studio or Vertex AI usage consumes credits instead of real billing. - Google AI Studio - Google AI Developers Forum\",\"url\":\"https://discuss.ai.google.dev/t/it-s-about-understanding-how-different-google-cloud-and-genai-credits-are-applied-which-services-they-cover-and-how-to-ensure-your-ai-studio-or-vertex-ai-usage-consumes-credits-instead-of-real-billing/138189\"},{\"title\":\"Google Developer Program Benefits FAQ | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/profile/help/benefits\"},{\"title\":\"Trial Credit for Genai App Builder | TikTok\",\"url\":\"https://www.tiktok.com/discover/trial-credit-for-genai-app-builder\"},{\"title\":\"Get a $1000 credit for Vertex AI Agent Builder - Tips & Tricks\",\"url\":\"https://community.n8n.io/t/get-a-1-000-credit-for-vertex-ai-agent-builder/48165\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about the Trial credit for GenAI App Builder and the $1000 promotional credit:\n\nGoogle Cloud offers a Gen AI Fast-Start Program that provides $1,000 trial credits for Vertex AI Agent Builder usage along with personalized workshops and technical consultations.\n\nThe Trial credit for GenAI App Builder has a validity period extending until April 2027.\n\nRegarding eligible products, for Google AI Studio, the credit can only be applied to Google GenAI models including Gemini 2.0+ models, and GenMedia models such as Imagen. However, the search results show some user confusion about which specific services are covered under the GenAI App Builder trial credit, with developers asking for clarification on whether it covers tools like Agent Builder, Search, and RAG services.\n\nThe search results indicate there are ongoing discussions in developer forums about how these credits work and which products are eligible, suggesting this information may vary or require direct confirmation from Google Cloud documentation.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"f7053288-1059-44ef-b30f-df047bcf750d","timestamp":"2026-05-10T01:55:58.657Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c23078aa-6f2d-40e2-86b4-48fcc37005bd","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"d60d1a13-7d3b-4659-b711-33fc77344be2","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"13d226c2-7030-46b3-a4a1-d92d92be18ee","agentId":"a6c3a5f3d9dc7d7f6","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UBgWESdLSuUXZMjVfJQgTf","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Google Cloud \"GenAI App Builder\" trial credit Vertex AI Agent Builder eligible services\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"No one is talking about how to use the Credits of Trial credit for GenAI App Builder - Gemini API - Google AI Developers Forum\",\"url\":\"https://discuss.ai.google.dev/t/no-one-is-talking-about-how-to-use-the-credits-of-trial-credit-for-genai-app-builder/101423\"},{\"title\":\"It’s about **understanding how different Google Cloud and GenAI credits are applied, which services they cover, and how to ensure your AI Studio or Vertex AI usage consumes credits instead of real billing. - Google AI Studio - Google AI Developers Forum\",\"url\":\"https://discuss.ai.google.dev/t/it-s-about-understanding-how-different-google-cloud-and-genai-credits-are-applied-which-services-they-cover-and-how-to-ensure-your-ai-studio-or-vertex-ai-usage-consumes-credits-instead-of-real-billing/138189\"},{\"title\":\"Google Developer Program Benefits FAQ | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/profile/help/benefits\"},{\"title\":\"Agent Search pricing | Google Cloud\",\"url\":\"https://cloud.google.com/generative-ai-app-builder/pricing\"},{\"title\":\"Accelerate Generative AI Adoption with Google Cloud\",\"url\":\"https://cloudcredits.io/providers/gcp/programs/google-cloud-gen-ai-fast-start-program\"},{\"title\":\"Google Cloud GenAI App Builder trial credit usage?\",\"url\":\"https://www.facebook.com/groups/vibecodinglife/posts/1992759101312617/\"},{\"title\":\"Get a $1,000 credit for Vertex AI Agent Builder - Tips & Tricks - n8n Community\",\"url\":\"https://community.n8n.io/t/get-a-1-000-credit-for-vertex-ai-agent-builder/48165\"},{\"title\":\"Gemini Enterprise Agent Platform (formerly Vertex AI) | Google Cloud\",\"url\":\"https://cloud.google.com/products/gemini-enterprise-agent-platform\"},{\"title\":\"Google AI Studio do not use my $1300 credits shown on Google Cloud - Gemini API - Google AI Developers Forum\",\"url\":\"https://discuss.ai.google.dev/t/google-ai-studio-do-not-use-my-1300-credits-shown-on-google-cloud/140442\"},{\"title\":\"SKU Groups - Google Developer Program Premium GenAI Credit | Google Cloud\",\"url\":\"https://cloud.google.com/skus/sku-groups/google-developer-program-premium-genai-credit\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about Google Cloud's GenAI App Builder trial credits and Vertex AI Agent Builder:\n\n## Trial Credit Programs\n\nGoogle Cloud offers $1,000 trial credits for Vertex AI Agent Builder usage as part of their GenAI Fast Start Program, which includes personalized workshops and technical consultations for enterprises exploring generative AI.\n\n## Eligible Services for GenAI Developer Credits\n\nThe GenAI credits may only be used in Google AI Studio and Google Cloud Vertex AI. More specifically:\n\n- For Google AI Studio, the credit can only be applied to Google GenAI models including Gemini 2.0+ models, and GenMedia models such as Imagen.\n- For Google Cloud Vertex AI, the credit can only be applied to Google GenAI models including Gemini 2.0+ models, and GenMedia models such as Imagen and Veo.\n\n## New Customer Credits\n\nAdditionally, new customers get up to $300 in free credits to try Agent Platform and other Google Cloud products.\n\nThe search results indicate there has been some confusion among developers about how to apply these different credit types, as these are separate promotional offerings with different eligibility requirements and applicable services.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"4c3de60b-eb2b-42ff-9584-a3cf5ea38279","timestamp":"2026-05-10T01:55:59.090Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d60d1a13-7d3b-4659-b711-33fc77344be2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"14ee6130-83d9-4cf3-ac06-2bce8a2ea26c","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"13d226c2-7030-46b3-a4a1-d92d92be18ee","agentId":"a6c3a5f3d9dc7d7f6","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014vT8rXc1DKfRjvw7gJ4EFR","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Gemini 2.5 Pro pricing Vertex AI vs Google AI Studio per million tokens 2026\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Google Vertex AI Pricing: Complete Enterprise Guide (2026)\",\"url\":\"https://www.cloudzero.com/blog/google-vertex-ai-pricing/\"},{\"title\":\"Gemini Developer API pricing | Gemini API | Google AI for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/pricing\"},{\"title\":\"Gemini API Pricing 2026: Complete Cost Guide for All Models | MetaCTO\",\"url\":\"https://www.metacto.com/blogs/the-true-cost-of-google-gemini-a-guide-to-api-pricing-and-integration\"},{\"title\":\"Vertex AI Pricing\",\"url\":\"https://cloud.google.com/vertex-ai/generative-ai/pricing\"},{\"title\":\"Gemini Pricing in 2026 for Individuals, Orgs & Developers\",\"url\":\"https://www.finout.io/blog/gemini-pricing-in-2026\"},{\"title\":\"Gemini Pricing 2026: Plans, API & Workspace Cost Guide\",\"url\":\"https://felloai.com/gemini-pricing/\"},{\"title\":\"Gemini API Pricing Calculator & Cost Guide (May 2026)\",\"url\":\"https://costgoat.com/pricing/gemini-api\"},{\"title\":\"Gemini API Pricing 2026: Complete Per-1M-Token Cost Guide with Calculator - All 7 Models Compared | Free Tier Details | Cost Optimization Tips | AI Free API\",\"url\":\"https://www.aifreeapi.com/en/posts/gemini-api-pricing-2026\"},{\"title\":\"Vertex AI Pricing: The Complete 2026 Guide to Costs, Hidden Fees, and Savings\",\"url\":\"https://www.nops.io/blog/vertex-ai-pricing/\"},{\"title\":\"Google AI Studio Pricing 2026: Free Tier, API Costs & Plans\",\"url\":\"https://www.nocode.mba/articles/google-ai-studio-pricing\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's the pricing comparison for Gemini 2.5 Pro across Vertex AI and Google AI Studio per million tokens in 2026:\n\n## Gemini 2.5 Pro Pricing\n\n**Standard Context (≤200K tokens):**\nGemini 2.5 Pro costs $1.25 per million input tokens and $10.00 per million output tokens on both platforms.\n\n**Extended Context (>200K tokens):**\nLarge context windows (200K-1M tokens) double those rates, bringing costs to $2.50 per million input tokens and $20.00 per million output tokens.\n\n## Key Differences Between Platforms\n\nVertex AI adds enterprise features: SLAs, Provisioned Throughput, VPC Service Controls, and compliance certifications compared to Google AI Studio.\n\n**Google AI Studio:**\nGoogle AI Studio usage is free of charge in all available regions for the interface itself, though the Gemini API pricing applies when used for production.\n\n**Pricing Parity:**\nPrices may differ from the prices listed here and the prices offered on Vertex AI. For Vertex prices, see the Vertex AI pricing page. However, the base token rates for Gemini 2.5 Pro are the same across both platforms at standard context rates.\n\n**Cost Optimization:**\nBatch API pricing cuts input token costs by 50% and output token costs by 50% compared to real-time inference, available on both platforms.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"212157a2-3089-4fe2-b692-7e4f03e8b7e6","timestamp":"2026-05-10T01:56:01.746Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"14ee6130-83d9-4cf3-ac06-2bce8a2ea26c","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"57eef0f8-82f1-43fa-be44-5b7541ec88d2","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"13d226c2-7030-46b3-a4a1-d92d92be18ee","agentId":"a6c3a5f3d9dc7d7f6","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Aaz6qHhFtbiXkMJRMoY7zE","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"OpenEvolve codelion Vertex AI Gemini backend support config\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"OpenEvolve: An Open Source Implementation of Google DeepMind's AlphaEvolve\",\"url\":\"https://huggingface.co/blog/codelion/openevolve\"},{\"title\":\"codelion/openevolve: Open-source implementation of ...\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/codelion/openevolve\"},{\"title\":\"codelion/openevolve | DeepWiki\",\"url\":\"https://deepwiki.com/codelion/openevolve\"},{\"title\":\"Releases · algorithmicsuperintelligence/openevolve\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/codelion/openevolve/releases\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - celerycelery/openevolve: Open-source implementation of AlphaEvolve · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/celerycelery/openevolve\"},{\"title\":\"OpenAI compatibility | Generative AI on Vertex AI | Google Cloud Documentation\",\"url\":\"https://docs.cloud.google.com/vertex-ai/generative-ai/docs/start/openai\"},{\"title\":\"Configure Gemini capabilities | Generative AI on Vertex AI | Google Cloud Documentation\",\"url\":\"https://docs.cloud.google.com/vertex-ai/generative-ai/docs/live-api/configure-gemini-capabilities\"},{\"title\":\"Add google-vertex-openapi provider for third-party models (GLM) · Issue #10304 · anomalyco/opencode\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/issues/10304\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - algorithmicsuperintelligence/openevolve: Open-source implementation of AlphaEvolve · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/algorithmicsuperintelligence/openevolve\"},{\"title\":\"Examples and Use Cases | codelion/openevolve | DeepWiki\",\"url\":\"https://deepwiki.com/codelion/openevolve/7-examples-and-use-cases\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about OpenEvolve's support for Gemini models through Vertex AI and its configuration options:\n\n## OpenEvolve Backend Support for Gemini via Vertex AI\n\nOpenEvolve uses the OpenAI SDK, so you can use any LLM or provider that supports an OpenAI compatible API. This means Vertex AI's Gemini models can be integrated through their OpenAI-compatible endpoint.\n\n## Configuration for Gemini Models\n\nOpenEvolve supports advanced LLM ensemble configuration with Gemini models, allowing specification of multiple models like \"gemini-2.5-pro\" and \"gemini-2.5-flash\" with weighted model selection.\n\nExample configuration for Gemini:\nThe configuration includes LLM ensemble setup with models specified by name and weight, temperature settings, database parameters for population management, evaluator settings, and prompt configuration options.\n\n## Vertex AI OpenAI Compatibility\n\nFor using Vertex AI with OpenAI-compatible clients, you can configure the OpenAI client with a base_url pointing to the Vertex AI endpoint and use Google Cloud authentication with access tokens. Compatible Gemini models available through Vertex AI can be selected from the models that Vertex hosts.\n\nThe configuration in OpenEvolve supports flexible LLM provider setup through standard OpenAI-compatible APIs, making it straightforward to integrate Vertex AI's Gemini backend.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"628d30f7-7a3e-4822-9379-9b77c557287b","timestamp":"2026-05-10T01:56:02.492Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"57eef0f8-82f1-43fa-be44-5b7541ec88d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
